      "worked_solution": "The bisector of an angle divides the angle into two congruent angles. Each of these congruent angles has a measure that is half the measure of the larger bisected angle. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC & =\\frac{m∠AOB}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{58}^{∘}}{2} \\\\  & ={29}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
